1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:12,262
[Julio] <i>You're an extraordinary woman.</i>

3
00:00:12,345 --> 00:00:14,681
<i>You showed admirable courage.</i>

4
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:18,685
<i>Our family is truly grateful</i>
<i>to you, Miss Aguas.</i>

5
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:20,729
<i>We are forever indebted.</i>

6
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:23,606
<i>I became a murderer</i>
<i>because of my love for you!</i>

7
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:26,693
<i>You didn't think about</i>
<i>how that affected Diego.</i>

8
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:30,947
<i>You killed his best friend!</i>
<i>You wiped out an entire family!</i>

9
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:34,909
[Jepoy] <i>I found the hitman Emilia hired.</i>
<i>He's alive.</i>

10
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:39,080
<i>I'll protect you.</i>
<i>I'll never leave your side.</i>

11
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:41,624
<i>Whatever happens, I won't leave you.</i>

12
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,960
<i>-Consider my investment done.</i>
<i>-Really?</i>

13
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:48,256
[Ivy] <i>Like what your mother,</i>
<i>the governor said, we're family now.</i>

14
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:52,802
[Loring] <i>The mayor wants to build</i>
<i>an export zone here</i>

15
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:54,971
<i>on the land owned by the cooperative!</i>

16
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:58,391
<i>And that Ivy? She's one of them!</i>
<i>She's an investor!</i>

17
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:00,977
<i>I want to host a fundraising dinner</i>

18
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,896
<i>-for the congressman.</i>
<i>-Fundraiser?</i>

19
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:05,231
[Diego] <i>Who gave you the right</i>
<i>to take the cooperative lot?</i>

20
00:01:05,315 --> 00:01:08,693
<i>Those peasants</i>
<i>will be compensated appropriately.</i>

21
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:10,862
Ivy, I know where they buried your mother.

22
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:12,405
<i>Where are you? I'm going there.</i>

23
00:01:12,489 --> 00:01:14,574
<i>I don't care about the Ardientes.</i>
<i>Where are you?</i>

24
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:15,950
[Jepoy] <i>Ivy, you have to face them.</i>

25
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:17,285
<i>Or your plans will be ruined.</i>

26
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:18,995
<i>The Ardientes are here.</i>

27
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:22,373
[Ivy] <i>I want you to remember my face.</i>

28
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:25,752
<i>I am Ivy Aguas.</i>

29
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:28,588
<i>And I am vengeance.</i>

30
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:32,801
[tense music playing]

31
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:37,430
[Raul] <i>You enjoyed murdering those people.</i>

32
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,766
<i>You wiped out an entire family.</i>

33
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:48,149
[Emilia] <i>Didn't you start all this?</i>

34
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:50,527
<i>If you hadn't taken</i>
<i>a liking to that girl's mother,</i>

35
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:53,822
<i>her father wouldn't have gone against us!</i>

36
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,743
[Arnaldo] <i>I want you</i>

37
00:01:58,827 --> 00:02:01,579
<i>to invest here in Ardiente.</i>

38
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,581
I'm planning to build
an export processing zone

39
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:05,792
<i>on the property we visited earlier.</i>

40
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:08,044
[tense music playing]

41
00:02:08,962 --> 00:02:12,882
[Julio] As long as this statue
stands firm in our town…

42
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,593
You will have leadership!

43
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:18,888
-Viva, Ardiente!
-[townsfolk] Viva, Ardiente!

44
00:02:18,972 --> 00:02:21,141
Viva, Ardiente!

45
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:22,976
[townsfolk] <i>Viva, Ardiente!</i>

46
00:02:25,186 --> 00:02:27,272
[Julio] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

47
00:02:27,355 --> 00:02:30,608
[townsfolk] <i>Long live, Ardiente!</i>

48
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:33,319
[tense music playing]

49
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:54,173
You're all murderers.

50
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:56,134
You're evil!

51
00:02:56,759 --> 00:02:59,971
You killed my parents!

52
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:03,558
So now I'll kill you all!

53
00:03:06,185 --> 00:03:09,105
One by one. You! You, Emilia.

54
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:13,234
You had my parents killed.

55
00:03:15,528 --> 00:03:17,322
-[gunshot]
-[screaming]

56
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:20,867
Emilia!

57
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:24,954
You bit--

58
00:03:25,038 --> 00:03:26,080
[gunshots]

59
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:28,958
[groans]

60
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:30,752
You started all this!

61
00:03:32,337 --> 00:03:33,963
-You bitch--
-[gunshots]

62
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,009
You murderers!

63
00:03:38,676 --> 00:03:40,595
You'll all pay!

64
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:42,513
-Especially you!
-[gunshots]

65
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:47,143
[tense music playing]

66
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:49,812
[sharp inhale]

67
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:51,522
You all deserve to die.

68
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,817
[tense music playing]

69
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:43,032
<i>No, Ivy. It shouldn't end like this.</i>

70
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:46,786
[dramatic music playing]

71
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:55,878
[gasps]

72
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,465
<i>I shouldn't stain my hands with blood.</i>

73
00:05:00,049 --> 00:05:02,802
<i>Mom and Dad wouldn't have wanted this.</i>

74
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,307
<i>Justice. Not revenge.</i>

75
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:09,642
<i>Just like what Ms. Prianka told me.</i>

76
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:12,687
Ivy?

77
00:05:15,356 --> 00:05:17,066
Ivy, is everything okay?

78
00:05:20,737 --> 00:05:23,239
Yes. Yes, Gov.

79
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:25,199
That's good to know.

80
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:27,327
Are you nervous for the event?

81
00:05:28,161 --> 00:05:29,203
[nervous sigh]

82
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:31,122
Don't be.

83
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:34,959
You're with the most
influential and successful family in town,

84
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:36,335
so you don't have to be nervous.

85
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:39,672
Come, let's meet your guests.

86
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:42,467
Congressman.

87
00:05:50,683 --> 00:05:53,644
Look at your tie!

88
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,355
Let's fix that.

89
00:05:56,439 --> 00:06:01,110
Diego, can you give me a ride?
Wait for me.

90
00:06:01,194 --> 00:06:03,154
Fernan invited us for some…

91
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:04,280
you know…

92
00:06:04,363 --> 00:06:05,698
[laughing]

93
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:09,368
-Sure, Uncle! I'll drop you off.
-All right. Thanks.

94
00:06:10,536 --> 00:06:12,080
Not too tight, okay?

95
00:06:12,163 --> 00:06:13,247
Diego…

96
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:17,293
Are you sure you want to go to this party?

97
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:20,880
The party is important to Mom.

98
00:06:20,963 --> 00:06:23,466
See? She even sent me some clothes.

99
00:06:23,549 --> 00:06:24,884
[chuckles]

100
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:27,762
Your mom sure knows how to convince you.

101
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:31,224
Just so she can get what she wants.

102
00:06:31,307 --> 00:06:32,725
As usual.

103
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:34,936
But don't worry.

104
00:06:35,019 --> 00:06:36,896
I won't pass up this chance.

105
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:41,818
I'll keep my eyes and ears open
for any news about Arnaldo's project.

106
00:06:44,153 --> 00:06:45,530
So, how do I look?

107
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:49,117
You're so handsome? Oh, don't forget this!

108
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:52,161
You have to wear this
to complete the look!

109
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,579
Oh, right.

110
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:58,000
My baby's so handsome!

111
00:06:58,084 --> 00:07:00,461
[applause]

112
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:02,380
Good evening, everyone.

113
00:07:02,463 --> 00:07:06,342
Thank you so much
for accepting my invitation.

114
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:11,681
For those who don't know me,
I am Ivy Aguas,

115
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:17,520
the owner and CEO
of Aguas Realty and Holdings, Inc.

116
00:07:17,603 --> 00:07:22,817
The leading realty company in the country.

117
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:26,446
Poblacion Ardiente has the potential

118
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:29,657
to become a mega-business hub.

119
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:34,495
And for the past 18 years,
it boasts a zero crime rate!

120
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:40,042
It really is inviting and enticing

121
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:43,546
to business owners like me.

122
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:45,089
[upbeat music playing]

123
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:47,884
And I just want you all to know that…

124
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:50,428
I want to be part of…

125
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:52,555
Ardiente's progress.

126
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:55,141
[applause]

127
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:58,603
Out with the old…

128
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:05,026
and in with… the new.

129
00:08:07,987 --> 00:08:09,572
New roads,

130
00:08:10,198 --> 00:08:11,699
new bridges,

131
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:13,075
commercial buildings,

132
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:15,286
five-star resorts…

133
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:18,998
the possibilities are endless
for Poblacion Ardiente,

134
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:21,125
and that is because of…

135
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:23,002
the brilliance…

136
00:08:23,085 --> 00:08:25,755
[tense music playing]

137
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:28,257
and diligence of…

138
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:29,509
our congressman.

139
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:32,803
I'll go ahead and call him Señor…

140
00:08:34,388 --> 00:08:36,098
Señor Julio.

141
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:39,352
Señor Julio…

142
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:40,478
Ardiente.

143
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:42,146
[applause]

144
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:53,407
So tonight,

145
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:56,619
I want you all to know that
in the upcoming elections,

146
00:08:57,245 --> 00:08:59,163
I will support…

147
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:04,043
Congressman Julio Ardiente
in his bid for the Senate.

148
00:09:05,711 --> 00:09:07,630
[applause]

149
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:14,720
And tonight,

150
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:16,180
we are all here…

151
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:18,057
because of an auction,

152
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,518
which profits will go

153
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:23,521
to the campaign fund of our congressman.

154
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:26,774
[applause]

155
00:09:30,069 --> 00:09:31,571
Congressman…

156
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:34,991
I mean…

157
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:36,826
Señor Julio…

158
00:09:38,869 --> 00:09:43,833
I hope this is the start
of our partnership.

159
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:48,629
Like they say in politics,

160
00:09:48,713 --> 00:09:51,924
it's not just about who wins.

161
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:55,219
Politics is about…

162
00:09:55,970 --> 00:10:00,266
making friends, finding your allies, and…

163
00:10:00,349 --> 00:10:02,560
destroying your enemies.

164
00:10:09,817 --> 00:10:11,152
Everyone…

165
00:10:15,114 --> 00:10:18,034
Let's make a toast
to Congressman Julio Ardiente,

166
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:22,538
our Señor Julio Ardiente,

167
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:25,458
and for Poblacion Ardiente…

168
00:10:26,792 --> 00:10:29,086
<i>And for my parents…</i>

169
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,172
Cheers!

170
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:35,134
-Cheers!
-Cheers.

171
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:36,802
Cheers.

172
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:52,109
[Pandoy laughs]

173
00:10:52,193 --> 00:10:54,195
[indistinct chatter]

174
00:10:54,278 --> 00:10:56,197
It looks like they're having fun already.

175
00:10:56,280 --> 00:11:00,076
[man] Don't worry.
I'll write this off your paycheck.

176
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:03,120
-Hey, save some for me!
-Hey, Pandoy! Diego!

177
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,623
[laughs]

178
00:11:06,332 --> 00:11:07,667
[man] Nice!

179
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:10,169
[Diego] It seems like everyone's early.

180
00:11:10,252 --> 00:11:11,754
I know. Shot, shot, shot, Diego. Shot.

181
00:11:11,837 --> 00:11:13,464
I can't. I have somewhere else to go.

182
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:16,092
[Pandoy] Let me chug that down for him.

183
00:11:16,175 --> 00:11:18,135
[laughing]

184
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:19,428
Here's to an abundant harvest!

185
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:21,389
To an abundant harvest!

186
00:11:21,472 --> 00:11:23,349
For the Ardientes!

187
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:24,600
Hold on…

188
00:11:24,683 --> 00:11:29,647
To the land they should've
given us long ago!

189
00:11:31,565 --> 00:11:33,692
Diego here's going to talk to the mayor

190
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:37,029
and the congressman
to stop the project here.

191
00:11:37,113 --> 00:11:40,157
That's why he's looking sharp,
because he's going to the party.

192
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:42,618
Don't worry. I'll have a talk with them.

193
00:11:42,701 --> 00:11:43,911
Diego!

194
00:11:43,994 --> 00:11:46,956
Don't listen to Pandoy. You know what?

195
00:11:47,039 --> 00:11:49,917
Attend that party. Who knows?

196
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,670
You might meet the woman for you there.

197
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:54,255
[man] That's right.

198
00:11:54,338 --> 00:11:55,297
[clears throat]

199
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:57,883
Or she could be right behind you.

200
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,552
-[man] Nice one!
-Nimfa!

201
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:01,429
[quiet music playing]

202
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:06,559
How did you manage to get Ms. Aguas?

203
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:07,935
[Pablo chuckles]

204
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:09,311
Julio, if I were you…

205
00:12:09,395 --> 00:12:11,689
I'd be insulted by that question.

206
00:12:11,772 --> 00:12:13,941
[laughs]

207
00:12:14,024 --> 00:12:16,152
I didn't mean to offend you, Congressman.

208
00:12:16,235 --> 00:12:17,486
[chuckles softly]

209
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:19,363
No offense taken. Um…

210
00:12:20,072 --> 00:12:21,615
If you add two million
to my campaign fund,

211
00:12:21,699 --> 00:12:23,909
I'll forget what you said.

212
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:27,580
[laughs]

213
00:12:27,663 --> 00:12:29,915
Now, kidding aside.

214
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:32,877
It was actually Miss Aguas who came to us

215
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,880
and told us
she was interested in investing

216
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:38,799
in the export processing zone
I'm putting up.

217
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:41,802
Interesting move.

218
00:12:41,886 --> 00:12:47,099
For a realtor to gamble in a

219
00:12:47,183 --> 00:12:49,602
public-private partnership that…

220
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:50,728
[huffs]

221
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,229
…is not even her line of business.

222
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:56,108
I mean, what's in it for her, Julio?

223
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:59,862
Well, to expand her business, of course.

224
00:13:00,488 --> 00:13:03,365
You know how these things work, senator.

225
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:04,909
An entrepreneur…

226
00:13:05,409 --> 00:13:10,289
will stick around
an influential politician of one province

227
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:12,666
to make their business prosper.

228
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:14,960
[tense music playing]

229
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:17,880
But just a piece of advice, Julio.

230
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:21,050
Be careful in dealing with her.

231
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:25,304
There's something about that woman.

232
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:26,972
You know what they say.

233
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:31,435
The butterfly only appears fragile.

234
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:34,313
[chuckling]

235
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:37,816
I didn't know you were

236
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,861
a psychic now, Senator.

237
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,863
[chuckling]

238
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:45,616
But, no really,

239
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,410
I appreciate your advice,

240
00:13:48,494 --> 00:13:49,620
so don't worry.

241
00:13:49,703 --> 00:13:51,247
I know what I'm doing.

242
00:13:52,915 --> 00:13:54,792
I'm Julio Ardiente.

243
00:13:55,292 --> 00:13:56,669
And I don't make mistakes.

244
00:13:56,752 --> 00:13:58,754
[dramatic music playing]

245
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:01,507
-[man] <i>Cheers!</i>
-[Diego] <i>Nimfa!</i>

246
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,259
-You're back?
-Get in!

247
00:14:03,342 --> 00:14:06,804
My contract in Manila ended.
My dad told me to stay here for now.

248
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:12,476
[Fernan] Right. Better here
than in Manila all by yourself!

249
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:15,104
Your mother and I will take care of you!

250
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:19,984
Wait. Diego, it's getting late.

251
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:23,237
Miss Ivy's party might be over
by the time you get there!

252
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:26,323
I know.

253
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:29,743
Hmm… So, you're going to a party.

254
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:33,038
-Here, Dad.
-My mom wanted me to go.

255
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:35,291
[indistinct chatter]

256
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:38,669
Well, I better go.

257
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:41,255
I'll update you guys about the project
they're planning to put up here.

258
00:14:41,338 --> 00:14:43,132
-Thanks, Diego!
-Sir, take care.

259
00:14:43,215 --> 00:14:45,134
-Stay safe.
-Take care.

260
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:47,052
-Uncle. Take it easy.
-Yeah?

261
00:14:47,136 --> 00:14:48,512
You're going to get it from Auntie later.

262
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:51,849
-He's a lightweight drinker.
-Nimfa.

263
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:55,311
-He's down in one shot.
-That's not true.

264
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:57,730
[man] He'll be out cold.

265
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:59,732
[Pandoy] No, I won't.

266
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:01,525
-I dare you.
-All right then.

267
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:03,652
-[men laughing]
-[indistinct chatter]

268
00:15:04,236 --> 00:15:06,989
-[man] Go on.
-[Pandoy] All right. Here we go.

269
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:12,870
[indistinct chatter]

270
00:15:12,953 --> 00:15:15,080
[Ivy] <i>We're going somewhere</i>
<i>after the party.</i>

271
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:17,833
<i>I want to see my mother.</i>

272
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:27,843
[indistinct chatter]

273
00:15:29,678 --> 00:15:32,097
Joan. Thank you.

274
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,726
-Mrs. Castro.
-Hi.

275
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:38,395
If you win the bidding,

276
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:39,855
I'll personally give you a tour.

277
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,941
Thank you, Ms. Aguas.

278
00:15:42,024 --> 00:15:45,444
You know,
what you're doing for Julio is nice here.

279
00:15:45,527 --> 00:15:47,655
But… I advise you

280
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:49,490
Advise what, Mrs. Castro?

281
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:52,993
Oh! Ah… Ma'am. Nothing, Gov. It's nothing.

282
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:55,037
Mrs. Castro…

283
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:58,415
when you say nothing,
it means there is something.

284
00:15:58,499 --> 00:15:59,625
Uh…

285
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,544
Gov, I'm sorry.

286
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:07,091
It was just a harmless comment. Sorry.

287
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:08,968
That's good to hear, Mrs. Castro.

288
00:16:09,635 --> 00:16:10,552
You know,

289
00:16:10,636 --> 00:16:14,473
spreading rumors
is like spreading infectious diseases.

290
00:16:15,265 --> 00:16:18,936
And do you know what should be
done with infectious diseases?

291
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:21,730
They should be eradicated!

292
00:16:22,731 --> 00:16:25,651
You know, because I don't
want my constituents to fall ill.

293
00:16:25,734 --> 00:16:27,611
[tense music playing]

294
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:29,238
Excuse me.

295
00:16:29,822 --> 00:16:31,115
Oh!

296
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,868
Did I just say something wrong?

297
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:36,578
[Emilia] Hmm…

298
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:38,497
Truth must have hurt.

299
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:42,584
You know, sometimes,
it's so hard being honest.

300
00:16:48,173 --> 00:16:49,091
You're right, Governor.

301
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:51,969
There aren't many honest people anymore.

302
00:16:52,052 --> 00:16:53,512
Like with men.

303
00:16:54,596 --> 00:16:57,016
They cheat so blatantly.

304
00:16:57,641 --> 00:17:00,019
[tense music playing]

305
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,484
That's why I don't easily trust men.

306
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:09,445
Men these days.

307
00:17:09,528 --> 00:17:11,155
If there are men that I do trust,

308
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:15,034
they would be Congressman Julio and…

309
00:17:15,117 --> 00:17:17,661
Mayor Ardiente-Torillo.

310
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:22,124
They are respectable
and won't ever trick you.

311
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:24,043
[Natalie] Exactly, Ivy.

312
00:17:24,626 --> 00:17:25,961
But apparently,

313
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:29,548
no matter how faithful your partner is,

314
00:17:29,631 --> 00:17:31,884
there are just some women

315
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:35,387
who can't stop until they ensnare them.

316
00:17:36,013 --> 00:17:37,931
That's why, Natalie…

317
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:40,851
keep your eyes peeled,
because someone might snatch him away.

318
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:43,270
Speaking of which…

319
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:44,980
the auction is about to start.

320
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:47,232
Excuse me, I better get ready.

321
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:49,568
[tense music playing]

322
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:11,548
[sinister music playing]

323
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,809
What a waste of money.

324
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:25,354
They should've donated it to the farmers.

325
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:33,153
I'm sorry!

326
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:39,535
Are you okay?

327
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:42,621
[tense music playing]

328
00:18:50,003 --> 00:18:51,046
Oh, hi.

329
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:52,506
-Hi.
-What's up?

330
00:18:52,589 --> 00:18:55,467
I guess we arrived too early. Right?

331
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:56,844
It's kind of boring here.

332
00:18:56,927 --> 00:18:59,054
We can go out, if you want.

333
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:01,390
[sinister music playing]

334
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:07,229
Thanks for the offer,

335
00:19:07,312 --> 00:19:09,189
but I'm with other people.

336
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,566
I'll go ahead.

337
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:15,737
My dear husband.

338
00:19:20,617 --> 00:19:22,286
-There you are.
-Yeah.

339
00:19:24,454 --> 00:19:27,499
And who are these quaint-looking models?

340
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:31,503
Oh, your dress looks beautiful,
ma'am. Where did you buy that?

341
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:34,339
Thank you. I got this
from a French designer.

342
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:37,217
Sadly, she passed away. You know why?

343
00:19:39,219 --> 00:19:42,806
She flirted with someone else's husband.

344
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:44,474
-Get it?
-[Raul] Let's go?

345
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:47,895
-We have to go.
-Yeah. Let's go, honey.

346
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:49,271
Oh!

347
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:53,734
By the way, it was nice meeting you both.

348
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:55,277
Take care out there.

349
00:20:01,283 --> 00:20:02,534
[Emilia] Let's go.

350
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:06,455
[instrumental theme music playing]

351
00:20:13,712 --> 00:20:15,505
Let me put these on you, dear.

352
00:20:20,302 --> 00:20:21,720
Ivy…

353
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:23,805
are you sure…

354
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,098
you're okay?

355
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:31,563
I want to go to my mom.

356
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:37,236
I want to visit her.

357
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:40,656
I know you're devastated, Ivy.

358
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:44,826
Let's just stop this party.
I'll ask them to leave.

359
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:48,747
I'll just tell them that
you're not feeling well, okay?

360
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:50,207
Dear?

361
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:55,504
If only we could.

362
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,096
But I have to push through.

363
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:08,392
I need to do this as part of my plan.

364
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:14,773
Ivy, in that case,

365
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:19,945
let out all your frustrations.

366
00:21:20,779 --> 00:21:22,656
Don't keep it in.

367
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:24,825
Or else, it'll eat you alive.

368
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:45,595
Thank you, Nanny.

369
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:49,224
For always being there.

370
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:53,729
I can do this, right?

371
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:56,648
Yes, dear.

372
00:21:57,649 --> 00:22:00,152
["Wildflower" by Arnel Pineda playing]
♪ <i>Let her cry</i> ♪

373
00:22:00,235 --> 00:22:04,573
♪ <i>For she's a lady</i>
<i>For she's a lady</i> ♪

374
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:08,201
♪ <i>Let her dream</i> ♪

375
00:22:08,285 --> 00:22:11,121
♪ <i>For she's a child</i>
<i>For she's a child</i> ♪

376
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:13,623
♪ <i>Let the rain fall down upon her…</i> ♪

377
00:22:27,971 --> 00:22:30,974
[flamenco music playing]

378
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:41,151
[Joan] Ladies and gentlemen,
Ms. Ivy Aguas.

379
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:47,843
[flamenco music playing]

380
00:25:12,385 --> 00:25:14,930
[applause]

381
00:25:25,899 --> 00:25:28,443
Ladies and gentlemen,
let the auction begin.

382
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:37,118
Our first property is in Batangas.

383
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:40,956
A beautiful two-story townhouse
situated by the sea.

384
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:43,792
It has three bedrooms,
two toilets and baths,

385
00:25:43,875 --> 00:25:45,168
and wrap-around balconies.

386
00:25:45,252 --> 00:25:48,088
Bidding starts at five million pesos.

387
00:25:48,171 --> 00:25:49,172
Five point five.

388
00:25:49,256 --> 00:25:52,259
[Joan] Five point five million pesos
for Mrs. De Castro.

389
00:25:52,342 --> 00:25:54,094
Do I hear

390
00:25:54,177 --> 00:25:55,262
six million?

391
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:59,391
-Six million.
-Six million for Mrs. Ramos.

392
00:25:59,474 --> 00:26:00,934
Anybody bidding higher?

393
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:04,980
Going once? Going twice?

394
00:26:05,063 --> 00:26:07,983
Sold to Mrs. Ramos for six million pesos.

395
00:26:08,066 --> 00:26:09,567
Congratulations, ma'am.

396
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:12,570
[applause]

397
00:26:14,572 --> 00:26:18,034
[Joan] We're very proud
to present our last property on the list.

398
00:26:18,118 --> 00:26:20,328
A secluded bed and breakfast

399
00:26:20,412 --> 00:26:23,915
overlooking
the cool mountains of Baguio City.

400
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:28,086
It boasts a café, a spa,
and a botanical garden.

401
00:26:28,169 --> 00:26:30,088
Bidding starts at 30 million pesos.

402
00:26:30,171 --> 00:26:33,216
-Thirty million.
-Thirty million for number seven.

403
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:34,301
[man] Thirty-two million.

404
00:26:34,384 --> 00:26:36,261
Thirty-two million for number five.

405
00:26:36,344 --> 00:26:37,637
Thirty-five million.

406
00:26:37,721 --> 00:26:40,015
Thirty-five million for the good senator.

407
00:26:40,098 --> 00:26:41,599
Thirty-seven million.

408
00:26:41,683 --> 00:26:44,978
Thirty-seven million, Mr. Romero.

409
00:26:45,770 --> 00:26:47,564
Thirty-eight million.

410
00:26:47,647 --> 00:26:51,026
[Joan] Thirty-eight million.
Anyone bidding higher?

411
00:26:52,277 --> 00:26:54,362
Thirty-eight million. Going once.

412
00:26:55,071 --> 00:26:56,239
Going twice.

413
00:26:56,323 --> 00:27:00,035
Sold to our dear Mr. Senator.
Congratulations, sir.

414
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:02,620
[applause]

415
00:27:05,165 --> 00:27:07,500
Thirty-eight million pesos
for such a small property?

416
00:27:09,836 --> 00:27:11,629
That could buy hectares of farmland.

417
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:14,007
[tense music playing]

418
00:27:20,513 --> 00:27:23,433
[Ivy] Thank you to everyone
who bid and won.

419
00:27:23,516 --> 00:27:27,896
This is a big help
for Congressman Ardiente

420
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:29,814
in his bid for the Senate.

421
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:31,524
[applause]

422
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:32,859
Congressman.

423
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:37,989
Ivy, if you don't mind,
could I say a few words?

424
00:27:38,698 --> 00:27:40,075
[Ivy] Um, sure.

425
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:41,868
I'll hold the mic for you.

426
00:27:42,619 --> 00:27:48,792
My friends, I would first like
to thank Ms. Aguas

427
00:27:49,459 --> 00:27:54,047
for insisting on organizing
this fundraising event.

428
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:57,592
This is a big help not just for me,

429
00:27:57,675 --> 00:28:01,262
but for all of us in Poblacion Ardiente.

430
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:03,056
[applause]

431
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:08,103
And aside from that,

432
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:11,106
I would like to personally thank

433
00:28:12,065 --> 00:28:13,566
Ms. Aguas…

434
00:28:13,650 --> 00:28:15,235
for her investment

435
00:28:15,318 --> 00:28:20,490
in the export processing zone
that will rise in our town.

436
00:28:20,573 --> 00:28:24,619
This project will be a big step

437
00:28:24,702 --> 00:28:27,622
in further promoting Poblacion Ardiente

438
00:28:27,705 --> 00:28:33,670
as the fruit and vegetable
export capital of our country.

439
00:28:33,753 --> 00:28:35,755
[applause]

440
00:28:37,298 --> 00:28:38,675
And of course,

441
00:28:38,758 --> 00:28:42,262
we are just waiting for additional funding

442
00:28:42,345 --> 00:28:45,223
to start the clearing
operations on the lot

443
00:28:45,807 --> 00:28:48,518
where this project will rise.

444
00:28:48,601 --> 00:28:51,855
And at this point,
not that I would like to put…

445
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:54,566
Ivy on the spot, but…

446
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:59,738
Can you further extend your assistance

447
00:28:59,821 --> 00:29:01,990
to Poblacion Ardiente?

448
00:29:04,242 --> 00:29:06,202
[somber music playing]

449
00:29:11,291 --> 00:29:13,042
[chuckles]

450
00:29:13,585 --> 00:29:15,920
Señor Julio…

451
00:29:17,088 --> 00:29:19,591
Señor Julio knows that…

452
00:29:21,801 --> 00:29:23,803
I just can't resist him!

453
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:24,971
[laughs]

454
00:29:25,054 --> 00:29:26,765
[Ivy] Of course, I will.

455
00:29:26,848 --> 00:29:28,850
Let's give Ivy a round of applause!

456
00:29:28,933 --> 00:29:29,893
[applause]

457
00:29:32,228 --> 00:29:33,730
Ladies and gentlemen,

458
00:29:33,813 --> 00:29:39,861
Ivy is such a generous person,
and she really loves Poblacion Ardiente.

459
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:43,740
With the blessing of what Ivy just said,

460
00:29:43,823 --> 00:29:47,660
our town's export processing zone

461
00:29:47,744 --> 00:29:50,997
is definitely a go.

462
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:53,166
Thank you, Ivy. Thank you very much.

463
00:29:53,249 --> 00:29:55,919
[applause]

464
00:29:56,002 --> 00:29:59,005
[tense music playing]

465
00:30:13,812 --> 00:30:16,147
We have a lot of projects…

466
00:30:16,981 --> 00:30:18,107
Miss, excuse me.

467
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:20,652
-[Ivy] Um…
-Excuse me.

468
00:30:21,653 --> 00:30:22,821
Let me guess…

469
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:26,533
-Mojito?
-That's too weak.

470
00:30:27,534 --> 00:30:29,244
I like it on the rocks.

471
00:30:29,327 --> 00:30:32,705
Oh. You really are something
else, Ms. Aguas.

472
00:30:33,289 --> 00:30:34,833
You know what you want.

473
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:38,461
Thank you for investing
in our project, by the way.

474
00:30:39,045 --> 00:30:40,964
I don't need your thanks.

475
00:30:41,548 --> 00:30:45,051
I invested a lot. That means, Mr. Mayor…

476
00:30:45,134 --> 00:30:47,720
I'll expect a lot in return.

477
00:30:48,763 --> 00:30:49,639
I know what you mean.

478
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:54,394
But can we not talk about business now?

479
00:30:56,729 --> 00:30:58,439
-Mr. Mayor--
-No, let's just…

480
00:30:59,023 --> 00:31:00,400
dance.

481
00:31:01,985 --> 00:31:03,444
After all…

482
00:31:03,528 --> 00:31:06,447
[sensual music playing]

483
00:31:08,032 --> 00:31:10,201
You're mesmerizing when you dance.

484
00:31:21,588 --> 00:31:22,797
Stop it.

485
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:26,885
If you don't want to be humiliated,
stop it, Mr. Mayor.

486
00:31:34,851 --> 00:31:37,312
-Ivy! Ivy!
-Mr. Mayor, what is your problem?

487
00:31:38,646 --> 00:31:41,941
Excuse me. What's going on?

488
00:31:44,235 --> 00:31:46,362
I need to talk to you, Arnaldo.

489
00:31:53,536 --> 00:31:54,996
Ms. Aguas.

490
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:56,831
I appreciate all the attention

491
00:31:56,915 --> 00:31:58,791
that you've been giving my boyfriend.

492
00:31:59,667 --> 00:32:03,212
You and I both know he is
so powerful and he's so handsome.

493
00:32:03,963 --> 00:32:06,466
And apparently,
every other girl in this town

494
00:32:06,549 --> 00:32:08,343
wants a taste of him.

495
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:13,014
But you know? My boyfriend is not a book

496
00:32:13,097 --> 00:32:14,349
nor is he a toy…

497
00:32:15,099 --> 00:32:16,768
that can be borrowed or shared.

498
00:32:16,851 --> 00:32:18,561
My boyfriend…

499
00:32:19,812 --> 00:32:21,105
is mine.

500
00:32:21,189 --> 00:32:23,191
Just mine.

501
00:32:24,442 --> 00:32:26,069
Do you understand?

502
00:32:26,152 --> 00:32:28,321
Completely, Natalie.

503
00:32:30,073 --> 00:32:32,367
Now listen to what I have to say.

504
00:32:33,743 --> 00:32:35,411
You can have Arnaldo.

505
00:32:35,995 --> 00:32:37,413
He's all yours.

506
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:39,749
I don't like secondhand things.

507
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:44,212
Because I like my toys brand new.

508
00:32:44,295 --> 00:32:47,882
[tense music playing]

509
00:33:00,311 --> 00:33:03,314
[tender music playing]

510
00:33:10,154 --> 00:33:11,864
[phone chimes]

511
00:33:16,244 --> 00:33:17,829
[Jepoy] <i>It's too dangerous.</i>

512
00:33:21,082 --> 00:33:22,750
[Ivy] <i>I want to see her.</i>

513
00:33:22,834 --> 00:33:24,502
<i>Take me to her.</i>

514
00:33:38,057 --> 00:33:40,226
<i>I need to talk to Grandpa.</i>

515
00:33:40,768 --> 00:33:42,687
<i>What will happen to the farmers?</i>

516
00:33:43,187 --> 00:33:45,106
<i>This is a huge problem.</i>

517
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:57,744
[Ivy gasps]

518
00:33:57,827 --> 00:34:00,872
[instrumental theme music playing]

519
00:34:03,499 --> 00:34:06,502
[theme music playing]

520
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:08,796
[young Ivy] <i>Hey kid, don't jump! Hey!</i>

521
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,673
[young Diego screaming]

522
00:34:10,757 --> 00:34:12,759
Help!

523
00:34:12,842 --> 00:34:14,260
[young Ivy] <i>Hang on!</i>

524
00:34:14,343 --> 00:34:16,471
-Careful, okay?
-Just hold on.

525
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:18,222
-Oh.
-[both chuckle]

526
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:20,016
[young Ivy laughs]

527
00:34:20,099 --> 00:34:23,019
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

528
00:34:23,102 --> 00:34:24,562
[snickers]

529
00:34:44,957 --> 00:34:46,626
[huffs and chuckles]

530
00:34:46,709 --> 00:34:47,752
I'm sorry.

531
00:34:49,420 --> 00:34:50,963
I'm sorry, Mr. Torillo.

532
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:52,965
I'm sorry for laughing. Um…

533
00:34:53,549 --> 00:34:56,010
I was caught off guard. Uh…

534
00:34:56,511 --> 00:34:58,930
What are you doing here, Mr. Torillo?

535
00:35:01,474 --> 00:35:03,684
Well… what are you doing here?

536
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:08,272
Why aren't you inside? It's your party.

537
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:14,445
Uh…

538
00:35:16,447 --> 00:35:18,574
I needed to take a call.

539
00:35:18,658 --> 00:35:20,451
It's noisy inside.

540
00:35:23,830 --> 00:35:27,250
I'm going back to the party now.

541
00:35:27,333 --> 00:35:28,876
Excuse me.

542
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:36,384
Miss Aguas. Hold on.

543
00:35:37,718 --> 00:35:39,554
How will you benefit…

544
00:35:39,637 --> 00:35:42,098
from investing in Ardiente?

545
00:35:49,230 --> 00:35:51,899
Never mind. I already know the answer.

546
00:36:08,291 --> 00:36:10,001
Ms. Aguas!

547
00:36:11,544 --> 00:36:13,045
Senator.

548
00:36:15,882 --> 00:36:17,175
Thirty-eight million.

549
00:36:18,092 --> 00:36:18,968
Ah.

550
00:36:19,594 --> 00:36:22,346
Thank you, Senator. You're too generous.

551
00:36:22,430 --> 00:36:25,141
Well, Julio and I are good friends.

552
00:36:25,224 --> 00:36:27,351
He helped me win in the last elections.

553
00:36:27,435 --> 00:36:30,730
And now it's my turn to help him.

554
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:35,401
Your friendship must run very deep.

555
00:36:35,484 --> 00:36:36,527
[chuckles]

556
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:38,362
Let's just say that…

557
00:36:38,446 --> 00:36:42,074
he knows me as well as I know him.

558
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:45,786
We protect each other.

559
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:47,580
[tense music playing]

560
00:36:47,663 --> 00:36:48,998
Oh.

561
00:36:49,999 --> 00:36:53,377
Your duo must be difficult
to beat, Senator.

562
00:36:53,461 --> 00:36:54,837
[chuckles]

563
00:36:54,921 --> 00:36:56,756
Don't worry, Miss Aguas.

564
00:36:58,132 --> 00:37:00,009
I won't get in the way…

565
00:37:00,635 --> 00:37:01,844
of your plans.

566
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:04,722
I'm sorry. Plans?

567
00:37:04,805 --> 00:37:06,182
[chuckles]

568
00:37:06,265 --> 00:37:08,976
Don't play coy with me, Miss Aguas.

569
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:10,019
[scoffs]

570
00:37:10,102 --> 00:37:12,188
You wouldn't invest that much money…

571
00:37:12,271 --> 00:37:14,357
for nothing.

572
00:37:16,442 --> 00:37:18,527
I know you're up to something.

573
00:37:20,780 --> 00:37:22,657
[tense music playing]

574
00:37:26,661 --> 00:37:32,291
Until we get the money
I made Miss Aguas hand over,

575
00:37:32,375 --> 00:37:34,335
we still have to reel her in.

576
00:37:35,586 --> 00:37:38,589
Why don't you invite her
for breakfast tomorrow at home?

577
00:37:38,673 --> 00:37:39,966
So we can

578
00:37:40,049 --> 00:37:42,260
finalize the papers for the projects.

579
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:44,679
I will, Papa. Leave it to me.

580
00:37:46,138 --> 00:37:47,098
[Ivy] <i>Senator.</i>

581
00:37:50,184 --> 00:37:52,561
You know us entrepreneurs too well.

582
00:37:54,438 --> 00:37:55,856
We're persuasive.

583
00:37:56,857 --> 00:37:58,442
-And clever.
-Oh.

584
00:37:58,526 --> 00:38:02,029
-[Pablo chuckles]
-When we do business. [chuckles]

585
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:04,448
I must say,

586
00:38:04,532 --> 00:38:08,202
you're a very
interesting woman, Miss Aguas.

587
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,537
[both chuckling]

588
00:38:09,620 --> 00:38:11,372
I envy Julio.

589
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:13,791
You chose him first.

590
00:38:15,084 --> 00:38:16,669
But just a fair warning.

591
00:38:18,504 --> 00:38:20,006
Be careful around Julio.

592
00:38:21,549 --> 00:38:24,927
He's clever too, like you.

593
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:27,138
[both chuckling]

594
00:38:27,221 --> 00:38:28,389
Senator,

595
00:38:29,348 --> 00:38:30,433
watch your words.

596
00:38:30,516 --> 00:38:33,352
The congressman's nearby.
I might tell on you.

597
00:38:33,436 --> 00:38:35,563
[both chuckles]

598
00:38:35,646 --> 00:38:38,774
-I like you, Ms. Aguas.
-And I like you too.

599
00:38:40,443 --> 00:38:43,529
Senator, I want to know more
about you and…

600
00:38:43,612 --> 00:38:46,240
Congressman Julio.
I hope we can talk sometime.

601
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:48,075
[chuckles] Sure.

602
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:51,162
-[chuckles]
-Anytime, Ms. Aguas.

603
00:38:51,912 --> 00:38:54,582
[tense music playing]

604
00:38:58,836 --> 00:39:02,465
Wait, where are Arnaldo and Diego?

605
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:05,634
There he is.

606
00:39:06,135 --> 00:39:07,553
Diego.

607
00:39:08,179 --> 00:39:09,347
Where's your necktie?

608
00:39:09,930 --> 00:39:12,641
I took it off, it's choking me.

609
00:39:12,725 --> 00:39:15,728
I don't care if it's choking you.

610
00:39:15,811 --> 00:39:17,813
This is a formal affair.

611
00:39:18,397 --> 00:39:20,733
You should look formal.

612
00:39:20,816 --> 00:39:23,736
Being with those farmers continues to

613
00:39:23,819 --> 00:39:26,072
diminish your breeding.

614
00:39:28,115 --> 00:39:29,992
Since you mentioned the farmers,

615
00:39:30,076 --> 00:39:32,536
I'm concerned about
what you said earlier, Grandpa.

616
00:39:32,620 --> 00:39:36,248
What will happen to the farmers
if you continue the project?

617
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:38,042
-Then they'll leave.
-But, Grandpa--

618
00:39:38,125 --> 00:39:39,710
Enough.

619
00:39:42,213 --> 00:39:44,215
Let's just talk about that
when we get home, okay?

620
00:39:44,298 --> 00:39:46,133
Where is Arnaldo?

621
00:39:46,217 --> 00:39:48,260
[Emilia] He should be here, Papa.

622
00:39:50,679 --> 00:39:52,556
-Oh.
-[Arnaldo] Where are you going?

623
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:54,266
We're going home.

624
00:39:54,350 --> 00:39:55,935
[speaker id] Let's go.

625
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:04,276
Papa, Arnaldo, go ahead.
I'll just ask Ivy something.

626
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:05,820
-Go ahead.
-Okay.

627
00:40:05,903 --> 00:40:06,946
All right.

628
00:40:09,448 --> 00:40:10,908
-[Carlotta and Emilia shrieking]
-Mom.

629
00:40:12,993 --> 00:40:14,578
Excuse me, Senator.

630
00:40:14,662 --> 00:40:15,871
-Sure.
-[Ivy] Joan?

631
00:40:15,955 --> 00:40:18,207
[screams]

632
00:40:18,916 --> 00:40:20,000
Emilia!

633
00:40:21,127 --> 00:40:22,211
Not this again.

634
00:40:24,046 --> 00:40:25,089
Ma'am…

635
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:27,133
-You okay, Mom?
-Ma'am, I'm sorry.

636
00:40:27,216 --> 00:40:28,134
[shrieking]

637
00:40:28,217 --> 00:40:29,427
-[Carlotta] Ouch!
-[Emilia gasps]

638
00:40:29,510 --> 00:40:30,636
-Ouch! My hand!
-Careful, ma'am.

639
00:40:30,719 --> 00:40:33,305
-[Carlotta yelping]
-[Emilia whimpers]

640
00:40:35,099 --> 00:40:37,601
I'll wrap this around your hand
to stop the bleeding.

641
00:40:37,685 --> 00:40:38,727
[Carlotta yelping]

642
00:40:38,811 --> 00:40:40,438
Please bear it.

643
00:40:41,397 --> 00:40:43,732
But you have to clean this later.

644
00:40:43,816 --> 00:40:45,776
Thank you, thank you.

645
00:40:45,860 --> 00:40:48,154
[Carlotta groaning]

646
00:40:48,237 --> 00:40:50,072
[yelping]

647
00:40:50,156 --> 00:40:52,116
-Thank you, sir.
-Nanny!

648
00:40:52,199 --> 00:40:54,118
Nanny Carlotta.

649
00:40:54,201 --> 00:40:55,870
What happened?

650
00:40:55,953 --> 00:40:57,288
Thank you, Mr. Torillo.

651
00:40:57,371 --> 00:40:59,373
What happened? How did it happen?

652
00:40:59,457 --> 00:41:01,167
Ivy, it was an accident!

653
00:41:01,792 --> 00:41:04,420
Your maid spilled hot coffee on me

654
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:06,922
then slipped on the ground
and hurt her hand!

655
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:09,008
Look at my skin now! It's irritated!

656
00:41:09,091 --> 00:41:10,426
What if I get first-degree burns?

657
00:41:10,509 --> 00:41:12,261
I have to go see
my dermatologist tomorrow.

658
00:41:12,344 --> 00:41:14,180
Ouch! Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch.

659
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:16,182
-[Emilia whimpers]
-[Carlotta groans]

660
00:41:16,265 --> 00:41:18,809
You've got the skin
of a crocodile, Governor.

661
00:41:18,893 --> 00:41:20,811
I'm sure it'll be okay.

662
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:22,188
You didn't get any cuts.

663
00:41:22,271 --> 00:41:24,356
[tense music playing]

664
00:41:29,487 --> 00:41:31,030
Next time, you be careful.

665
00:41:31,614 --> 00:41:34,408
You know, maids like you
should have presence of mind.

666
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:36,035
Especially you, you're old already.

667
00:41:36,118 --> 00:41:37,495
Who will hire you?

668
00:41:37,578 --> 00:41:39,914
What will happen to your family?

669
00:41:39,997 --> 00:41:43,292
I mean, you should be thankful
that Ivy's nice.

670
00:41:43,375 --> 00:41:45,836
If you worked for me,
I wouldn't allow this.

671
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:48,047
Use your head. You're so stupid!

672
00:41:48,130 --> 00:41:49,215
-Mom.
-That's enough, Governor.

673
00:41:57,431 --> 00:41:58,891
I'm…

674
00:41:58,974 --> 00:42:01,352
I'm sorry, Governor.
I'll talk to her myself.

675
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:05,689
But I'd never entrust…

676
00:42:05,773 --> 00:42:07,900
my house…

677
00:42:07,983 --> 00:42:09,193
and my life…

678
00:42:10,945 --> 00:42:13,989
to anyone I think is stupid.

679
00:42:16,450 --> 00:42:17,743
[exhales sharply]

680
00:42:20,496 --> 00:42:22,790
[music]

681
00:42:22,873 --> 00:42:26,126
I'm sorry. Don't get me wrong.

682
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:30,589
You know, she should be more careful.

683
00:42:30,673 --> 00:42:32,967
We can also be more careful…

684
00:42:33,050 --> 00:42:34,969
with the words we say.

685
00:42:37,054 --> 00:42:38,430
Right, Governor?

686
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:42,059
[clears throat]

687
00:42:44,103 --> 00:42:45,980
I'm sorry…

688
00:42:46,063 --> 00:42:47,565
but you may leave.

689
00:42:49,441 --> 00:42:51,026
[scoffs]

690
00:42:51,819 --> 00:42:53,571
Yeah, we better get going.

691
00:42:54,405 --> 00:42:55,531
We should go now.

692
00:42:56,865 --> 00:42:59,535
Oh, by the way, congratulations.

693
00:42:59,618 --> 00:43:02,663
Your event was such a huge success.

694
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:05,165
We'll go ahead.

695
00:43:06,458 --> 00:43:07,751
Oh.

696
00:43:08,252 --> 00:43:11,547
I shall see you tomorrow,
for breakfast in our house, right?

697
00:43:14,216 --> 00:43:15,301
And don't worry.

698
00:43:15,384 --> 00:43:17,303
My maids…

699
00:43:17,386 --> 00:43:19,305
won't spill coffee on you.

700
00:43:23,892 --> 00:43:25,269
Bye.

701
00:43:25,894 --> 00:43:28,689
[tense music playing]

702
00:43:35,863 --> 00:43:36,864
I'm sorry.

703
00:43:37,489 --> 00:43:38,490
Nanny…

704
00:43:48,709 --> 00:43:51,378
That maid ruined my dress!

705
00:43:51,462 --> 00:43:52,588
Ugh!

706
00:43:52,671 --> 00:43:54,340
I just had this made…

707
00:43:54,423 --> 00:43:55,758
and now it's ruined.

708
00:43:55,841 --> 00:43:56,884
Poor dress.

709
00:43:56,967 --> 00:43:59,637
So disgusting!

710
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:02,056
It stinks.

711
00:44:02,139 --> 00:44:05,059
It's just stained.
You can always buy a new one.

712
00:44:05,934 --> 00:44:07,227
Excuse me, Raul.

713
00:44:07,311 --> 00:44:09,647
My dress isn't like your women…

714
00:44:09,730 --> 00:44:11,398
cheap and disposable.

715
00:44:13,734 --> 00:44:17,237
Well? Aren't you going to say anything?

716
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:20,199
You know, Raul,
you're really unbelievable.

717
00:44:20,783 --> 00:44:22,409
You might be forgetting that

718
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:24,036
I am now the governor.

719
00:44:24,119 --> 00:44:26,497
So please act respectably.

720
00:44:26,580 --> 00:44:30,668
I know it's difficult for you,
but put in some effort.

721
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:32,795
Gosh.

722
00:44:35,089 --> 00:44:37,633
You know what, Emilia?
I haven't done anything wrong.

723
00:44:38,217 --> 00:44:40,761
I just talked to them. That's it.

724
00:44:40,844 --> 00:44:44,306
So, I don't understand
why you keep running your mouth.

725
00:44:45,265 --> 00:44:46,433
Hey.

726
00:44:47,017 --> 00:44:48,769
Where are you going now?

727
00:44:48,852 --> 00:44:50,229
Why are you packing your stuff?

728
00:44:50,312 --> 00:44:52,648
Are you going to see your mistress again?!

729
00:44:53,899 --> 00:44:55,317
No.

730
00:44:55,401 --> 00:44:59,113
I'll go earn some money
so you can buy a new dress.

731
00:45:00,030 --> 00:45:02,074
What? Ugh!

732
00:45:03,450 --> 00:45:04,451
My dress.

733
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:06,870
[whimpers]

734
00:45:09,623 --> 00:45:13,168
[somber music playing]

735
00:45:16,880 --> 00:45:18,090
Sweetie.

736
00:45:18,173 --> 00:45:19,800
Dear, that's enough.

737
00:45:22,010 --> 00:45:23,637
Ivy, dear.

738
00:45:24,847 --> 00:45:27,891
You shouldn't let
your anger get the best of you.

739
00:45:27,975 --> 00:45:30,310
You shouldn't have defended me.

740
00:45:30,394 --> 00:45:34,022
Emilia might
want to do something against you.

741
00:45:34,606 --> 00:45:37,025
Your plans will be ruined.

742
00:45:37,109 --> 00:45:38,944
Why wouldn't I defend you?

743
00:45:41,447 --> 00:45:45,159
Nanny, I'm sorry, but tomorrow,
you must go to Manila.

744
00:45:45,784 --> 00:45:47,411
Leave me here for now.

745
00:45:47,494 --> 00:45:48,704
No.

746
00:45:48,787 --> 00:45:50,998
I won't leave you here, Ivy.

747
00:45:51,081 --> 00:45:53,584
Please don't be stubborn.

748
00:45:53,667 --> 00:45:55,711
I don't want those Ardientes to hurt you.

749
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:57,504
You're the only family I have now.

750
00:45:57,588 --> 00:46:00,466
I… I don't know what I'd do if?

751
00:46:00,549 --> 00:46:03,469
Hush. Dear.

752
00:46:04,553 --> 00:46:06,263
Calm down.

753
00:46:06,346 --> 00:46:10,893
All that anger won't do you any good.

754
00:46:12,686 --> 00:46:14,146
I won't leave you.

755
00:46:14,229 --> 00:46:15,397
Nanny…

756
00:46:16,190 --> 00:46:18,400
-Look what happened to you.
-[shushes]

757
00:46:18,984 --> 00:46:20,319
Ivy…

758
00:46:20,402 --> 00:46:22,321
[tense music playing]

759
00:46:25,073 --> 00:46:26,700
You're okay now, right?

760
00:46:26,783 --> 00:46:28,368
-Mm-hmm.
-Get some rest.

761
00:46:28,452 --> 00:46:31,663
I have to go.
Let's go. Take me to my mother.

762
00:46:32,623 --> 00:46:33,749
But, Ivy…

763
00:46:35,542 --> 00:46:37,836
Take me to her.

764
00:46:37,920 --> 00:46:40,214
-Ivy.
-Get some rest.

765
00:46:40,297 --> 00:46:41,924
Jepoy, let's go.

766
00:46:42,758 --> 00:46:44,968
Well? Let's go!

767
00:46:45,052 --> 00:46:47,304
[tense music playing]

768
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:52,476
Je--

769
00:47:06,281 --> 00:47:08,116
[somber music playing]

770
00:47:24,049 --> 00:47:25,926
[gasping]

771
00:47:34,184 --> 00:47:35,727
Mom?

772
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:41,900
Mom?

773
00:47:47,114 --> 00:47:48,699
Mom…

774
00:47:52,995 --> 00:47:54,371
[crying]

775
00:48:00,627 --> 00:48:01,837
Mom, it's…

776
00:48:02,421 --> 00:48:05,007
Mom, it's me Lily.

777
00:48:06,592 --> 00:48:08,635
It's Lily, Mom.

778
00:48:08,719 --> 00:48:11,430
[instrumental theme music playing]

779
00:48:29,698 --> 00:48:30,782
[crying]

780
00:48:31,658 --> 00:48:32,576
Mom…

781
00:48:32,659 --> 00:48:35,746
[music continues]

782
00:48:35,829 --> 00:48:38,665
[Ivy wailing]

783
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:42,836
[crying] Mom…

784
00:48:42,919 --> 00:48:45,005
Mom…

785
00:48:45,088 --> 00:48:48,592
Jepoy, what did they do to my mother?!

786
00:48:49,718 --> 00:48:53,597
Jepoy, what did they do to her?

787
00:48:53,680 --> 00:48:55,641
Why did this happen?!

788
00:48:55,724 --> 00:49:01,813
How could they do this to her?

789
00:49:02,522 --> 00:49:05,108
What happened, Mom?

790
00:49:05,192 --> 00:49:07,903
Mom… What happened?

791
00:49:10,072 --> 00:49:13,950
Why did it happen, Jepoy?

792
00:49:18,246 --> 00:49:21,249
[instrumental theme music playing]

793
00:49:24,419 --> 00:49:27,130
[Diego] <i>I still believe there's</i>
<i>hope for this town.</i>

794
00:49:27,214 --> 00:49:29,883
<i>No matter what you do,</i>
<i>you can't change their lives</i>

795
00:49:29,966 --> 00:49:32,969
<i>as long as this family is in power.</i>

796
00:49:33,053 --> 00:49:39,184
[Ivy] <i>I feel nothing but pain,</i>
<i>hatred, and fury, Mom.</i>

797
00:49:39,267 --> 00:49:41,561
<i>I promise you and Dad.</i>

798
00:49:41,645 --> 00:49:43,772
<i>I'll avenge your deaths.</i>

799
00:49:43,855 --> 00:49:45,065
[Ivy screaming]

800
00:49:45,148 --> 00:49:48,068
<i>Governor, now that someone's</i>
<i>openly going against you,</i>

801
00:49:48,151 --> 00:49:49,903
<i>I'm starting to reconsider my investment.</i>

802
00:49:49,986 --> 00:49:53,740
<i>These things started</i>
<i>the moment she came here.</i>

803
00:49:53,824 --> 00:49:56,952
<i>I'll uncover her deepest secrets.</i>

804
00:49:57,035 --> 00:49:59,579
[theme music playing]
